    "field": "Aquatic biogeochemistry",
    "problem": "The significant contribution of greenhouse gas emissions from African inland waters to global carbon budgets is poorly quantified and understood, as previous global estimates have been hampered by an extreme scarcity of empirical data from the continent.",
    "method": "To quantify greenhouse-gas emissions, we measured dissolved carbon dioxide, methane, and nitrous oxide concentrations across 12 sub-Saharan African rivers, calculated fluxes using published gas transfer velocities, and upscaled these fluxes to the entire region using available spatial data sets.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify greenhouse gas (CO2, CH4, N2O) emissions from sub-Saharan African inland waters by measuring dissolved gas concentrations in 12 river basins, calculating fluxes, and upscaling these data to assess their significance for regional and global carbon budgets.",
